            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of acute coronary dissection by angioplasty during diagnostic catheterization by the Sones' technique].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>483-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Male, 50 year-old, white, who underwent coronary arteriography and exhibited proximal dissection of the left anterior descending coronary artery induced by the Sones catheter with subsequent acute vessel occlusion. The patient was immediately treated by balloon angioplasty with excellent outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
